  "gridSize": 18,
  "steps": [
    "The previous frame is the reference frame. The encoder divides it into 16 × 16 macroblocks.",
    "The current frame comes next in time. The ball moved one macroblock to the right.",
    "Motion estimation starts. The encoder selects one macroblock to encode, M_T.",
    "The encoder looks at the same place in the reference frame. It sets a search region around that place.",
    "The encoder compares M_T with each candidate block in the search region. It keeps the block with the smallest difference.",
    "The best match is M_R. The motion vector V points from the old place to M_R.",
    "The encoder sends only V and the difference M_D = M_T − M_R. The DCT and the coder make M_D small.",
    "Motion compensation: the decoder copies M_R from the reference frame, moves it by V and adds M_D. This gives M_T again."
  ],
